      },
      "hints": [
        "Form the two vectors from the vertex of the required angle: $\\overrightarrow{AM}=2\\mathbf j+\\mathbf k$ and $\\overrightarrow{AP}=-2\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j+2\\mathbf k$.",
        "Use $\\overrightarrow{AM}\\cdot\\overrightarrow{AP}=|AM||AP|\\cos\\angle PAM$.",
        "Calculate the dot product and both magnitudes, then apply inverse cosine in the desired angular unit."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Find the vector $\\vec{AM} = \\vec{OM} - \\vec{OA}$:\n$$\\vec{AM} = (3\\mathbf{i} + 2\\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k}) - 3\\mathbf{i} = 2\\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k}$$",
        "Find the vector $\\vec{AP} = \\vec{OP} - \\vec{OA}$ using point $P(1, 1, 2)$:\n$$\\vec{AP} = (\\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j} + 2\\mathbf{k}) - 3\\mathbf{i} = -2\\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j} + 2\\mathbf{k}$$",
        "Compute the scalar product $\\vec{AM} \\cdot \\vec{AP}$:\n$$\\vec{AM} \\cdot \\vec{AP} = (0)(-2) + (2)(1) + (1)(2) = 0 + 2 + 2 = 4$$",
        "Compute the magnitudes of $\\vec{AM}$ and $\\vec{AP}$:\n$$|\\vec{AM}| = \\sqrt{0^2 + 2^2 + 1^2} = \\sqrt{5}$$\n$$|\\vec{AP}| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + 1^2 + 2^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 1 + 4} = \\sqrt{9} = 3$$",
        "Calculate $\\cos\\angle PAM$:\n$$\\cos\\angle PAM = \\dfrac{\\vec{AM} \\cdot \\vec{AP}}{|\\vec{AM}||\\vec{AP}|} = \\dfrac{4}{3\\sqrt{5}} \\approx 0.596285$$",
        "Find angle $PAM$:\n$$\\angle PAM = \\cos^{-1}(0.596285) \\approx 53.4^\\circ \\quad (\\text{or } 0.932 \\text{ radians})$$"
      ],
