      },
      "hints": [
        "A general point $Q$ on the line through $O$ and $M$ has position vector $\\mu(3\\mathbf i+2\\mathbf j+\\mathbf k)$.",
        "Form $\\overrightarrow{PQ}=\\mu(3\\mathbf i+2\\mathbf j+\\mathbf k)-(\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j+2\\mathbf k)$.",
        "At the perpendicular foot, impose $\\overrightarrow{PQ}\\cdot(3\\mathbf i+2\\mathbf j+\\mathbf k)=0$ and solve for $\\mu$.",
        "Substitute this value into $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ and take its magnitude, leaving the length exact."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Write the vector equation of the line passing through $O$ and $M$ with direction vector $\\mathbf{d} = 3\\mathbf{i} + 2\\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k}$:\n$$\\mathbf{r} = \\mu(3\\mathbf{i} + 2\\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k})$$",
        "Let $Q$ be the foot of the perpendicular from $P(1, 1, 2)$ on the line $OM$:\n$$\\vec{OQ} = 3\\mu\\mathbf{i} + 2\\mu\\mathbf{j} + \\mu\\mathbf{k}$$",
        "Form the vector $\\vec{PQ} = \\vec{OQ} - \\vec{OP}$:\n$$\\vec{PQ} = (3\\mu - 1)\\mathbf{i} + (2\\mu - 1)\\mathbf{j} + (\\mu - 2)\\mathbf{k}$$",
        "Apply the perpendicularity condition $\\vec{PQ} \\cdot \\mathbf{d} = 0$:\n$$3(3\\mu - 1) + 2(2\\mu - 1) + 1(\\mu - 2) = 0$$\n$$(9\\mu - 3) + (4\\mu - 2) + (\\mu - 2) = 0$$\n$$14\\mu - 7 = 0 \\implies \\mu = \\dfrac{1}{2}$$",
        "Substitute $\\mu = \\dfrac{1}{2}$ into $\\vec{PQ}$:\n$$\\vec{PQ} = \\left(\\dfrac{3}{2} - 1\\right)\\mathbf{i} + \\left(1 - 1\\right)\\mathbf{j} + \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2} - 2\\right)\\mathbf{k} = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{i} + 0\\mathbf{j} - \\dfrac{3}{2}\\mathbf{k}$$",
        "Calculate the exact length of the perpendicular $|\\vec{PQ}|$:\n$$|\\vec{PQ}| = \\sqrt{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^2 + 0^2 + \\left(-\\dfrac{3}{2}\\right)^2} = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{1}{4} + \\dfrac{9}{4}} = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{10}{4}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}$$"
      ],
